==Trivia==
*In the [[Nyanko Daisensou|Japanese version]], this stage takes place in '''Tottori Prefecture'''.
**In the [[Battle Cats (Removed Game)|original English version]], it was mistranslated as '''Shimatori'''.
*Madagascar's [[Treasure]] is an [[wikipedia:Aye-aye|aye-aye]], a species of primate native to Madagascar.
*Tottori Prefecture's base looks like some kind of ''[[wikipedia:Yōkai|yōkai]]'', a class of supernatural entities and phenomena in Japanese folklore. This may be an indirect reference to the [[wikipedia:GeGeGe no Kitarō|''GeGeGe no Kitarō'']] franchise, which features many one-eyed ''yōkai'' and whose author, [[wikipedia:Shigeru Mizuki|Shigeru Mizuki]], grew up in Tottori. There's even a ''GeGeGe no Kitarō''- and ''yōkai''-themed road dedicated to him: [[wikia:gegegenokitaro:Shigeru Mizuki Road|Shigeru Mizuki Road]].
**The ''yōkai'' it most resembles is [[wikipedia:Hitotsume-kozō|''hitotsume-kozō'']], but there isn't anything in its folklore connecting it to Tottori Prefecture. Thus, it is more likely just a generic ''yōkai'' made as an allusion to ''GeGeGe no Kitarō''.

